##

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:03.695 position:72% line:91%
We're about to do a fight scene,
which means I need to give you the disclaimer.

00:00:03.695 --> 00:00:06.468 position:56% line:91%
This is Jill Bearup,
extremely qualified actor-combatant,

00:00:06.468 --> 00:00:08.507 line:91%
with years of experience
and a YouTube channel,

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:11.368 line:91%
where she breaks down fight scenes
and does experiments with swords.

00:00:11.368 --> 00:00:15.357 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>We have had several days of rehearsal.
We have a fight coordinator on set.</c>

00:00:15.357 --> 00:00:18.202 line:91%
<c.yellow>We have a lot of people doing
a lot of things to keep us safe.</c>

00:00:18.202 --> 00:00:20.736 line:91%
So please,
do not try this at home.

00:00:21.412 --> 00:00:22.284 line:85%
Woah!

00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:24.515 line:85%
Ack!

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.022 line:91%
<c.yellow>Tom and I are shooting
a fight scene,</c>

00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:39.839 line:91%
<c.yellow>which culminates in him
getting thrown out the window.</c>

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:43.079 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>So he's coming into my bar,
and I don't want him there,</i></c>

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:45.480 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>because he's barred,
we have a fight about it,</i></c>

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.455 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>I smash a bottle over his head,</i></c>

00:00:47.455 --> 00:00:50.364 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>put his hat back on him,
and chuck him through a window.</i></c>

00:00:50.364 --> 00:00:52.986 line:91%
<c.yellow>He's probably feeling terrified.
I would be.</c>

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.776 line:85%
<c.yellow>But, he's gonna do great.</c>

00:01:10.362 --> 00:01:14.370 line:91%
<c.cyan>A newbie like Tom,
it starts from the first warmup.</c>

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.777 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>I start warming them up,
and I start seeing their mobility,</i></c>

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.633 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>their general confidence,
their energy levels.</i></c>

00:01:22.839 --> 00:01:24.277 line:85%
Gaah!

00:01:25.131 --> 00:01:26.270 line:85%
<i>(cackles)</i>

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.470 line:91%
<c.cyan>And then I start to think,
are there any moves</c>

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.786 line:91%
<c.cyan>that I've planned,
that this will facilitate?</c>

00:01:30.786 --> 00:01:32.746 line:91%
<c.cyan>Are there any moves
that we could really show off</c>

00:01:32.746 --> 00:01:35.232 line:85%
<c.cyan>this element of physicality?</c>

00:01:35.232 --> 00:01:36.720 line:85%
<c.cyan>And with Tom...</c>

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.929 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>I was going into this thinking,</i></c>

00:01:38.929 --> 00:01:40.885 position:56% line:85%
<c.cyan><i>"We're gonna have to be very simple.</i></c>

00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:42.909 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>"We're gonna have to cut
a lot of the choreography out."</i></c>

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:44.593 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>It's gonna have to be very short."</i></c>

00:01:44.593 --> 00:01:47.911 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>And... within the first
few hours of day one,</i></c>

00:01:47.911 --> 00:01:51.047 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>he'd pretty much nailed
— not to performance speed —</i></c>

00:01:51.047 --> 00:01:54.781 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>but nailed the choreography
of the hardest phrase in the fight.</i></c>

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.554 position:58% line:91%
<c.cyan>And at that point, I was like,
"We're not gonna have an issue here."</c>

00:01:57.554 --> 00:01:59.677 line:91%
There's a lot to remember,
from a novice's perspective,

00:01:59.677 --> 00:02:03.384 line:91%
'cause I've got to...
not only remember the choreography,

00:02:03.384 --> 00:02:06.648 line:91%
and remember,
eye contact before each thing,

00:02:06.648 --> 00:02:08.782 line:91%
so we know we're both ready.
<c.yellow>Yep.</c>

00:02:08.782 --> 00:02:10.604 line:85%
But also to remember performing.

00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:13.432 line:85%
Like, I've gotta just not be...

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:15.086 line:85%
<i>running through the moves.</i>

00:02:15.086 --> 00:02:17.148 line:91%
<i>I've gotta make sure my face
is doing the right thing as well.</i>

00:02:17.148 --> 00:02:18.895 line:85%
<i>There's a lot to cover.</i>

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:21.511 line:91%
When you do this on a stage...
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:02:21.511 --> 00:02:23.796 line:91%
You don't get multiple takes.
That's terrifying.

00:02:23.796 --> 00:02:26.716 line:91%
<c.yellow>You do not.
But we rehearse it.</c>

00:02:26.716 --> 00:02:30.001 line:91%
<c.yellow>We rehearse the scene as much as
we rehearse the choreography.</c>

00:02:30.001 --> 00:02:33.306 line:91%
<c.yellow>So you learn the moves,
and you get them into your brain,</c>

00:02:33.306 --> 00:02:34.808 line:91%
<c.yellow>and then the next day,
you come in and go,</c>

00:02:34.808 --> 00:02:37.725 line:91%
<c.yellow>"Right, what are the lines,
and how do they fit in?"</c>

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:42.014 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>There are three things,
which people are scared of.</i></c>

00:02:42.014 --> 00:02:45.901 position:69% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>Especially if, like you or me,
when you start, you've never done it before.</i></c>

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:50.195 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>You're scared of hurting yourself,
you're scared of hurting other people,</i></c>

00:02:50.195 --> 00:02:52.146 position:59% line:85%
<c.yellow><i>and you're scared of them hurting you.</i></c>

00:02:52.146 --> 00:02:56.044 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow>In choreography, there's usually
one thing which will get you bruises.</c>

00:02:56.044 --> 00:02:58.512 line:91%
<c.yellow>Not because you're
hitting each other very hard...</c>

00:02:58.512 --> 00:03:01.524 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow>but because you're hitting each other
not very hard, repeatedly.</c>

00:03:01.524 --> 00:03:03.201 line:85%
Yeah, this arm, this arm.

00:03:03.201 --> 00:03:05.486 line:91%
<i>You've gotta wail on this arm
like three times.</i>

00:03:05.486 --> 00:03:07.980 line:91%
<i>And I've gotta remember to react.
That's the thing.</i>

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.334 line:91%
'Cause I'm just there going,
"Ehh, ehh."

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:13.757 position:63% line:91%
And it's like, "Oh, no. I've gotta react
like you're really hitting me there."

00:03:13.757 --> 00:03:14.259 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yep.</c>

00:03:14.259 --> 00:03:16.244 line:91%
And I'm gonna forget
to do that at least once.

00:03:16.244 --> 00:03:17.173 line:85%
<c.yellow>It's okay.</c>

00:03:17.173 --> 00:03:19.071 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>Like, it's all in the reaction, really.</i></c>
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:03:19.071 --> 00:03:22.099 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>Because, the reaction is
how you make me look good.</i></c>

00:03:22.099 --> 00:03:23.939 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>And the reactions are
how I make you look good.</i></c>

00:03:23.939 --> 00:03:24.749 line:85%
<i>'Kay.</i>

00:03:24.749 --> 00:03:25.825 line:85%
D'oh!

00:03:26.482 --> 00:03:29.937 line:91%
<c.cyan>So, aside from things like
victim control...</c>

00:03:31.679 --> 00:03:34.048 line:91%
Yep.
<c.cyan>...and contact...</c>

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:37.800 position:56% line:91%
Could've warned me!
<c.cyan>...we have a couple of other ways...</c>

00:03:38.263 --> 00:03:41.390 line:91%
<c.cyan>of making— <i>(wheezes)</i></c>
<c.cyan>of making real things fake.</c>

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:44.214 line:91%
<c.cyan>First one is distance —
we change the distance,</c>

00:03:44.214 --> 00:03:46.406 line:91%
<c.cyan>from what would
actually be a punch in the face,</c>

00:03:46.406 --> 00:03:49.126 line:91%
<c.cyan>so that this punch is not going
far enough to hit Jill.</c>

00:03:50.389 --> 00:03:52.267 line:91%
<c.cyan>Okay.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>So worst case, I can't hit you.</c>

00:03:56.309 --> 00:03:59.247 line:91%
<c.cyan>The other one's displacement.
So what we're doing here...</c>

00:03:59.247 --> 00:04:02.028 line:91%
<c.cyan>is imagining that there's
a parrot sat on Jill's shoulder,</c>

00:04:02.028 --> 00:04:03.567 line:85%
<c.cyan>and Tom's gonna knock it out.</c>

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.762 position:56% line:91%
<c.cyan>And if the timing of the interaction
matches up,</c>

00:04:05.762 --> 00:04:08.227 line:91%
<c.cyan>it should look like
it's just popped her in the nose,</c>

00:04:08.227 --> 00:04:09.595 line:85%
<c.cyan>and she's gone backwards.</c>

00:04:11.273 --> 00:04:14.015 line:91%
<c.cyan>There we go.
Now if we turn 90 degrees...</c>

00:04:14.015 --> 00:04:16.870 line:91%
Yeah. That's not gonna work.
<c.cyan>we see that Tom is actually...</c>

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:20.001 line:91%
<c.cyan>not looking at Jill at all.
He's looking over her shoulder.</c>

00:04:20.001 --> 00:04:23.228 line:91%
I still need to make eye contact,
to cue the things that happen.

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:25.528 line:91%
<c.cyan>To make sure that she's happy to
go ahead with this move.</c>

00:04:31.279 --> 00:04:33.436 line:91%
<c.yellow>So in addition to
distance and displacement</c>

00:04:33.436 --> 00:04:36.091 line:91%
<c.yellow>— which we use as much as possible,
because they're the safest —</c>

00:04:36.091 --> 00:04:40.200 line:91%
<c.yellow>we have victim control,
which is bio-mechanical tricking.</c>

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:45.155 line:91%
<c.yellow>I have this.
I am not holding onto Tom at all.</c>

00:04:45.155 --> 00:04:47.423 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'm not doing anything.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>There's nothing there.</c>

00:04:47.423 --> 00:04:50.198 line:85%
<c.yellow>I'm letting him lead me around,</c>

00:04:50.198 --> 00:04:52.865 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>but making it look like
I'm leading him.</i></c>

00:04:52.865 --> 00:04:56.693 line:91%
<i>You are the line of safety
for yourself and for me.</i>

00:04:56.693 --> 00:04:58.120 line:85%
<i>I'm hopefully gonna remember</i>

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.086 line:91%
distancing and displacement,
and everything like that.

00:05:01.086 --> 00:05:03.910 position:69% line:91%
I'm terrified I'm not going to.
I'm terrified I'm gonna hit you in the face.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.894 line:85%
<c.yellow>I know how far away you are,</c>

00:05:05.894 --> 00:05:08.356 line:91%
<c.yellow>and I don't have to
close my eyes at any point.</c>

00:05:08.356 --> 00:05:11.984 line:85%
<c.yellow>So, if you get it wrong...</c>

00:05:11.984 --> 00:05:15.609 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>even if that take is scrubbed, like,
you're not gonna hit me in the face.</c>

00:05:15.609 --> 00:05:17.847 line:91%
Okay.
<c.yellow>'Cause I know where you are...</c>

00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:20.175 line:91%
<c.yellow>...and I will move.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Okay.</c>

00:05:20.175 --> 00:05:23.919 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow><i>If you trust yourself, then you know
where you are in space,</i></c>

00:05:23.919 --> 00:05:25.572 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>and you know
where your partner is,</i></c>

00:05:25.572 --> 00:05:27.677 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>and so you know that
you're safe,</i></c>

00:05:27.677 --> 00:05:30.184 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>because even if
they do something wrong,</i></c>

00:05:30.184 --> 00:05:31.448 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>you can move.</i></c>

00:05:32.266 --> 00:05:33.955 line:85%
Whoa, hold it.

00:05:33.955 --> 00:05:36.510 line:91%
<c.yellow><i>You can get closer,
the more you trust each other.</i></c>

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:38.572 line:85%
<c.yellow>I absolutely trust Tom.</c>

00:05:39.462 --> 00:05:40.812 line:91%
<c.yellow>And—</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Thank you.</c>

00:05:40.812 --> 00:05:43.615 line:91%
I don't trust me! <i>(laughs)</i>
<c.yellow>You're fine, you're fine!</c>

00:05:43.615 --> 00:05:44.658 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>(chuckles)</i></c>

00:05:45.227 --> 00:05:46.792 align:start size:88% position:13% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>♪ (upbeat country music)</i></c>

00:05:52.815 --> 00:05:55.260 line:91%
I feel like
I wanna try something more.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.600 align:start size:88% position:13% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>(music ends)</i></c>

00:06:00.214 --> 00:06:02.197 line:85%
Ohh! <i>(chuckles)</i>

00:06:04.602 --> 00:06:08.149 line:91%
Seeing it on there is—
It's brilliant.

00:06:09.085 --> 00:06:10.465 line:85%
This is fun, Jill!

00:06:10.465 --> 00:06:11.727 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>(giggles)</i></c>

00:06:11.727 --> 00:06:12.528 line:85%
<c.yellow>Told you!</c>

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.400 align:start size:88% position:13% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>♪ (music restarts)</i></c>

00:06:12.528 --> 00:06:16.846 line:91%
<c.yellow>Thought I told you...
to stay out of my bar!</c>

00:06:16.846 --> 00:06:19.372 line:91%
So I'm kicking...
not getting that high.

00:06:19.372 --> 00:06:21.631 line:85%
I'm kicking 'bout...

00:06:21.631 --> 00:06:22.894 line:85%
<c.cyan>Keep kneeling.</c>

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:24.718 line:85%
<c.green>Action.</c>

00:06:26.036 --> 00:06:27.093 line:85%
Guh!

00:06:27.093 --> 00:06:30.851 line:91%
<c.yellow>Told you, you're not
welcome in my bar!</c>

00:06:30.851 --> 00:06:32.670 line:85%
You moved!

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.600 align:start size:88% position:13% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>(music ends)</i></c>

00:06:35.593 --> 00:06:39.277 position:58% line:68%
<c.green><i>When we're doing a fight scene,
we need to really consider the space.</i></c>

00:06:39.277 --> 00:06:41.778 position:56% line:91%
<c.green>Like, as a director, I'm making sure
that the framing of it</c>

00:06:41.778 --> 00:06:45.720 position:64% line:91%
<c.green>includes everything in terms of location,
but isn't so tight that</c>

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.022 line:91%
<c.green><i>the camera might get hit
when they're actually fighting.</i></c>

00:06:48.022 --> 00:06:50.062 position:58% line:91%
<c.green><i>So when we're positioning the camera,
we need to make sure that</i></c>

00:06:50.062 --> 00:06:51.801 line:91%
<c.green><i>we're giving them enough space
to move around</i></c>

00:06:51.801 --> 00:06:53.707 position:58% line:85%
<c.green><i>without also sort of pulling punches,</i></c>

00:06:53.707 --> 00:06:55.382 line:91%
<c.green><i>because they think
they might hit the camera.</i></c>

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.025 line:85%
<c.cyan>Weapons are on set now.</c>

00:06:58.025 --> 00:07:01.136 line:91%
<c.cyan>We are treating them as though
they are live, sharp, and steel.</c>

00:07:01.136 --> 00:07:03.327 line:91%
<c.cyan>Even though they're plastic,
they're still pointy.</c>

00:07:03.327 --> 00:07:05.811 line:91%
<c.cyan>And just for good practice,
just for good practice,</c>

00:07:05.811 --> 00:07:07.918 line:91%
<c.cyan>we're gonna treat these
like they're live. Okay?</c>

00:07:07.918 --> 00:07:11.704 size:84% position:58% line:91%
Dodging the knife, right.
Dodging the knife, left.

00:07:11.704 --> 00:07:13.427 size:88% position:56% line:91%
Get kicked,
move out of the way,

00:07:13.427 --> 00:07:16.890 line:91%
block the stab,
grab the knife, reverse it,

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:19.185 line:85%
take the knife, hold it...

00:07:19.185 --> 00:07:22.752 line:91%
<c.yellow>Ideally, the consequences,
if you don't do the move correctly,</c>

00:07:22.752 --> 00:07:24.503 line:91%
<c.yellow>are that you stop it
halfway through.</c>

00:07:24.503 --> 00:07:27.458 line:91%
<c.yellow>So if you saw me
forget to kick Tom,</c>

00:07:27.458 --> 00:07:31.302 line:91%
<c.yellow>and then... come in
for a stab around,</c>

00:07:31.302 --> 00:07:32.950 line:85%
<c.yellow>I stopped before I got to him,</c>

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:36.755 line:91%
<c.yellow>because I realise that
he hadn't actually moved.</c>

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:39.595 line:91%
We're both aware of
each other's positions.

00:07:39.595 --> 00:07:42.364 line:91%
And if the other person's
not in the right place,

00:07:42.364 --> 00:07:44.450 position:58% line:85%
we can't really make the eye contact,

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.790 line:91%
like the cue... manoeuvre...
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:50.208 line:91%
that tells our opponent,
"We're okay to move."

00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:54.039 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah. Like, the thing that I like most
about stage combat is basically:</c>

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:56.788 line:91%
<c.yellow>You don't have an opponent.
You have a partner.</c>

00:07:56.788 --> 00:08:00.212 line:91%
<c.yellow>And your job is to make them
look as badass as possible.</c>

00:08:00.212 --> 00:08:02.411 line:91%
<c.yellow>And hopefully, they are doing
the same thing for you.</c>

00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:05.765 position:64% line:91%
<c.cyan>Well, you're both looking badass,
so you're obviously both doing your jobs.</c>

00:08:05.765 --> 00:08:06.771 line:85%
One person is.

00:08:10.639 --> 00:08:12.679 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(clank, rip)</i></c>

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:17.859 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(solid knocks)</i></c>

00:08:18.677 --> 00:08:20.277 line:7%
<c.green>Keeping the natural posture</c>

00:08:20.001 --> 00:08:20.973 line:85%
I'm exhausted.

00:08:20.277 --> 00:08:21.877 line:7%
<c.green>just means that you can come out...</c>

00:08:21.607 --> 00:08:23.203 line:85%
I'm absolutely exhausted.

00:08:23.203 --> 00:08:25.507 line:91%
I've got one more in me,
then we need to break for lunch.

00:08:25.507 --> 00:08:27.676 line:91%
I don't know about Jill.
<c.yellow>Yep, that sounds good to me.</c>

00:08:27.676 --> 00:08:28.375 line:85%
Okay.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:50.512 line:91%
Nope.
<c.yellow>Nope.</c>

00:08:50.512 --> 00:08:51.887 line:91%
You okay?
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:08:51.887 --> 00:08:55.162 position:59% line:91%
<c.cyan>All this movement is
victim-controlled, including the jump,</c>

00:08:55.162 --> 00:08:58.646 position:56% line:91%
<c.cyan>but because the jump
could benefit from, like, an assist,</c>

00:08:58.646 --> 00:09:00.802 line:91%
<c.cyan>we're having Tom put
a little bit of lift in there,</c>

00:09:00.802 --> 00:09:03.687 line:91%
<c.cyan>as Jill is jumping,
and Tom's just assisting.</c>

00:09:03.687 --> 00:09:06.248 line:91%
